---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Write for Code Coffee Break"
  description="A contribution guide for practical engineering articles: real problems, clear decisions, useful code, and evidence."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <h1>Share something useful.</h1>
      <p>
        A problem you solved, an experiment you ran, or a tool you built. Give
        another developer something they can use.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/templates/article.md" download>
        Download the draft template <Icon name="arrow" size={13} />
      </a>
    </header>
    <article class="page-body prose">
      <h2>What fits here</h2>
      <p>
        Debugging stories, architecture decisions, hands-on tutorials, build
        logs, and measured experiments. Pick one concrete problem and explain
        what made it interesting.
      </p>
      <h2>Show your work</h2>
      <p>
        Include enough context for someone else to follow: the constraints, the
        approach, what worked, and what you would change. Code should be
        runnable or clearly marked as a shortened example. Measurements need a
        method and units.
      </p>
      <p>
        Use public or synthetic examples. Link sources for external claims,
        credit collaborators, and distinguish observed results from estimates.
        Keep customer data and employer-confidential details out of the draft.
      </p>
      <h2>Keep your own voice</h2>
      <p>
        Write like you are explaining it to a colleague. A short, specific
        article is welcome. Your name stays on your work. Disclose AI assistance
        and label illustrative examples.
      </p>
      <h2>Preparing a contribution</h2>
      <p>
        The template is Markdown. Replace the prompts, add your author name and
        a useful summary, then keep it in draft until the examples and
        conclusions are ready.
      </p>
      <h2>Submissions</h2>
      <p>
        Community submissions are not open yet. The contribution guide and
        template are available now; a submission destination will be linked here
        when it is ready.
      </p>
      <p>
        In the meantime, <a href="/articles">read the articles</a>,{' '}
        <a href="/tools">try a tool</a>, or{' '}
        <a href="/rss.xml">follow new writing via RSS</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
